DESCRIPTION:Spend Earth Day 2026 with us here at the North Carolina Zoo!\n\
 n\nBring us your old cell phones\, tablets or other hand-held electronics 
 to the Zoo to recycle at the Gorilla habitat! Zoo Staff and Keepers will b
 e at the Gorilla Habitat overlook from 10 a.m. - 2 p.m. where you can recy
 cle your old electronic device and learn about how recycling old electroni
 cs can directly impact gorillas in the wild! We can help you declutter and
  you help preserve wild gorilla habitat! \n\n\nStop by Kidzone from 10 a.m
 . - 2 p.m. in North America to participate in the City Nature Challenge Bi
 oBlitz. Participants will earn native pollinator seeds and possibly even a
  pollinator plant to take home. We will have tablets with iNaturalist on t
 hem so guests can see how it works and can practice on native wildlife in 
 Kidzone. We’ll have lots of NC native Animal Ambassadors throughout the 
 day and tables where guests can learn more about the different types of an
 imals (and plants) that they may find. \n\n\nBoth of these events are free
  with Zoo admission. Happy Earth Day!
GEO:35.629422;-79.764409
LOCATION:North Carolina Zoo
SUMMARY:Earth Day at the Zoo 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/earth-day-at-the-zoo
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Nature & Wildlife Programs
END:VEVENT
