DESCRIPTION:NC State Parks is offering a free combination canoe paddle and 
 cleanup at the Lower Haw River State Natural Area on Earth Day. Paddle the
  Haw in a tandem canoe while cleaning up trash in the river along the way.
  After a short introduction\, the paddle trip will launch at Bynum Mill Ac
 cess and take out about 3.4 miles downstream at the US 64 Haw River Canoe 
 Access\, with a shuttle ride back to Bynum Mill Access. Bring your own sna
 cks/lunch and drinking water for a short lunch stop along the river. NC St
 ate Parks will provide the canoes\, life jackets\, and shuttle ride.  Esti
 mated total time for event including introduction\, lunch stop\, paddling\
 , and shuttle ride back is approximately 4 hours total. Guide is Sean Higg
 ins\, Interpretation & Education Manager with NC State Parks. For question
 s\, contact Sean Higgins at sean.higgins@ncparks.gov. Space is limited to 
 10 people. Pre-registration required.  Sign up at this link:  https://form
 s.gle/qJdBqhd4Vyqk4RVK6
GEO:35.771669;-79.142253
LOCATION:Lower Haw River SNA - Bynum Mill Access
SUMMARY:NC the Beautiful: Earth Day Canoe Paddle & Cleanup
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/earth-day-canoe-paddle-clean
 up
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Outdoor Recreation (kayak\, paddle\, hikes)
