UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_50921813037828
DTSTART:20260423T130000Z
DTEND:20260424T130000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Brunswick County Master Gardeners Volunteer Association wil
 l hold an online plant sale starting on April 17\, 2026 and running until 
 April 24\, 2026 with pick up day on May 1\, 2026. This event celebrates th
 e important colonial history of Brunswick County  through education on her
 bs\, flowers\, vines\, shrubs and small trees which thrive here. Plants fe
 atured are those which our Colonial ancestors would have encountered along
  our coast and the Cape Fear River which are native to our region and supp
 ort pollinators. Also featured will be plants from seeds which colonists b
 rought with them from Europe and plants which recognize the contributions 
 and life celebrations of the Gullah Geechee people who were enslaved in Af
 rica to work the rice plantations along the Cape Fear River. This online p
 lant sale celebrates the cultural traditions  found in gardening in our co
 astal region of the State.
GEO:34.056715;-78.165769
LOCATION:Pick up 5/1/26 at Greenhouses behind Building N
SUMMARY:Celebrating Our Colonial Roots - Online Plant Sale
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/celebrating-our-colonial-roo
 ts-online-plant-sale
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
END:VEVENT
