DESCRIPTION:Join us for a living history event that will provide a comprehe
 nsive view of maritime history within the region\, provide context for nav
 al stores production along the lower Cape Fear\, and provide interpretatio
 ns of eighteenth century trades that are relevant to maritime history and 
 sailing. It will contextualize the role of the naval stores industry in Br
 unswick's development as a major colonial port. This is a free event for a
 ll ages.
GEO:34.040206;-77.946023
LOCATION:Brunswick Town/Fort Anderson
SUMMARY:Between the Devil and the Deep Blue Sea: Sailors and Tar Workers in
  the 18th Century
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/between-the-devil-and-the-de
 ep-blue-sea-sailors-and-tar-workers-in-the-18th-century
