DESCRIPTION:Join the Museum of the Albemarle on Saturday\, Apr. 25 from 10
 –11:30 a.m. to celebrate National Coin Week as we explore the world of c
 oins and their history. The theme this year is “Striking Independence: 2
 50 Years of American Numismatics.” Learn about the change in your pocket
 \, discover coins from around the globe\, and uncover the wonders of coin 
 collecting with this free hands-on workshop for families. The workshop inc
 ludes coins and collecting resources for children to take with them. This 
 program is designed for grades 1–5.\n\n \n\nRegistration is required\, a
 s space is limited. To register\, call 252-331-4054 or email noah.janis@dn
 cr.nc.gov.\n\n \n\nThe Museum of the Albemarle\, a part of the Division of
  State History Museums\, Office of Archives and History\, is an agency of 
 the North Carolina Department of Natural and Cultural Resources.
GEO:36.296532;-76.219757
LOCATION:Museum of the Albemarle\, Ferebee Classroom
