DTSTAMP:20260522T042636Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52640478143107
DTSTART:20260425T150000Z
DTEND:20260425T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us as the community of Norwood and Stanly County commemora
 tes the Revolutionary Battle of Colson's Mill that occurred July 21\, 1780
 .  A mural depicting this battle was designed and painted by local mural a
 rtists\, Jack and Eli Williams of Williams Brothers Murals\, Albemarle\, N
 C. \n\nColson’s Mill was one of the first Patriot victories in the South
 ern Campaign of the American Revolution. It encouraged other Colonists to 
 support the American War of Independence.\n\nAfter the victory at Colson
 ’s\, the winds of war shifted with subsequent victories at Kings Mountai
 n and Cowpens. The wider campaign continued through Guilford Courthouse\, 
 and ultimately\, Yorktown\, where the British surrendered.\n\nWho are the 
 artists of the Colson Mill mural?\n\nWMS Brothers\, Jack and Eli Williams 
 were born and raised in Albemarle\, NC\, and grew up with an art-teacher a
 s a father. Their love of painting was sparked at a young age. They began 
 creating large-scale work in 2015\, but officially started painting murals
  in 2020. Each brother brings their our own strengths but combine them int
 o one collaborative voice.\n\nArtist Vision for the Battle of Colson’s M
 ill mural:\n\n“This piece is an abstract interpretation of the Battle at
  Colson’s Mill. Our inspiration came from the cubist art style. We used 
 sharp angles\, broken shapes\, and bold color block to capture the chaos\,
  speed\, and intensity of the battle.\nOn the left\, the blue forms with w
 hite marks represent the Patriot militia. On the right\, the reds and oran
 ges symbolize the Loyalists. The mill sits at center of the mural. The flo
 wing shapes along the bottom of the mural represent the meeting point of t
 he Pee Dee River and Rocky River.\nThe entire composition is meant to feel
  loud and full of motion.”\n\nThis mural was funded by a grant from Amer
 ica 250 NC.
GEO:35.225422;-80.120008
LOCATION:Outdoor Art Gallery
SUMMARY:Battle of Colson's Mill - Mural Unveiling
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/battle-of-colsons-mill-mural
 -unveiling
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
END:VEVENT
