DESCRIPTION:Join us to commemorate the surrender negotiations at Bennett Pl
 ace that led to the largest surrender of the American Civil War. Learn mor
 e about how Generals Johnston and Sherman's three meetings at the Bennetts
 ' home reflected the broader national debate over how to reunite the natio
 n & remake the United States without slavery. Explore how veterans\, civil
 ians\, and freed people alike experienced and thought about the end of the
  American Civil War and what would come next.\n\nThis program includes sev
 eral costumed interpretation events and displays.\n\nTickets must be purch
 ased on site the day of the event.\n\nSchedule of Events:\n\nTalks & Prese
 ntations\n\n11:00  The Road to Bennett Place - Ranger Talk\n\n12:00  "Civi
 l War Railroads in NC: Development & Impact on the War" - Presentation by 
 Dr. Ted Kunstling\, MD (Raleigh Civil War Round Table President)\n\n1:00* 
  The Story from the Land - Environmental History Walking Tour (*time may c
 hange)\n\n2:00  Surrender & Freedom Stories - Presentation\n\n2:30  What C
 omes Next?: Aftermath of the Civil War - Ranger Talk\n\nSurrender Vignette
 s 11:30\, 11:50\, 12:10\, 1:20\, and 1:40\n\nLimited spaces available insi
 de the Bennett home! Be in the room where it happened while our site histo
 rians walk through the surrender negotiations. Features Sherman and Johnst
 on reenactors. (15 minutes) Advance registration link via Eventbrite - som
 e tickets available same-day. Advanced registration recommended.\n\nFree F
 lowing Stations Explore at your own pace from 11:00 - 3:00. Most stations 
 include hands-on education.\n\nCivil War EngineeringSignal FlagsMorse Code
 Civilians on the HomefrontUS & Confederate soldiers at the end of the warP
 lease note due to the current drought\, there will be no hearth or campsid
 e cooking demonstrations.
GEO:36.029293;-78.975047
LOCATION:Bennett Place State Historic Site
SUMMARY:Uneasy Peace: 161st Anniversary Commemoration
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/uneasy-peace-161st-anniversa
 ry-commemoration
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Special Site Programs
END:VEVENT
