DESCRIPTION:The 2026 NCSciFest theme is "Science Matters" and we're excited
  to talk about eleven years of bluebird conservation lessons learned by st
 aff & volunteers at Haw River State Park. Meet in the courtyard outside of
  the Main Lodge (building closest to flagpole) for a talk about the histor
 y of bluebird conservation followed by an easy hike around Lake Loop (0.7 
 miles) to view several different styles of nestboxes and look for baby bir
 ds. Please bring comfortable walking shoes for a natural-surface travel (p
 acked dirt or gravel) and water/snacks as needed. Don't miss out on this o
 pportunity to connect with nature and expand your knowledge of the local w
 ildlife as we celebrate science in the outdoors!
