DESCRIPTION:Please note: this event has been rescheduled from March 28 to A
 pril 25.\n\nCelebrate spring with an immersive afternoon of Persian classi
 cal and folk music and dance. We have gathered Iranian musicians\, a dance
 r\, and a visual artist from across North America to create a breathtaking
  journey through the elegant beauty of Persian art. This performance blend
 s original music\, dance\, and visual art to explore the rich and diverse 
 folk traditions from different regions of Iran.\n\nAbout NCMA Sacred Song 
 Series\nThis series features music inspired by global faith traditions\, b
 ringing to life the diversity of religious expression in our region and th
 e NCMA collection. Performances include both traditional and contemporary 
 music\, ranging from Persian-Jewish piyyut (liturgical poems) to Sufi raga
 s to Black gospel.\n\nProgram\n\nPart 1: Sayeh Ensemble (45 min.)\n• Mah
 ya Hamedi\, vocals\n• Hamed Tabkhi\, tar\n• Pouya Shabanpour\, tonbak/
 daf\n• Dorsa Davoodabadi\, dance\n• Behzad Riyazi\, visual art\n• Pe
 ter Sumner\, cello\n\nIntermission (10–15 min.)\n\nPart 2: Special Guest
  Performance (30 min.)\nWe are pleased to have a renowned Persian tar play
 er and her husband perform.\n• Sahba Motallebi\, tar\n• Reza Mohsenipo
 ur\, tar
GEO:35.807856;-78.703922
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art
SUMMARY:NCMA Sacred Song Series: Persian Nowruz (New Year) Celebration
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ncma-sacred-song-series-pers
 ian-nowruz-new-year-celebration
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
CATEGORIES:Concerts (Music)
