DESCRIPTION:The new Introduction to Woodworking class teaches beginners to 
 safely and efficiently use hand and power tools\, understand different woo
 d types and their properties\, and apply fundamental techniques like cutti
 ng\, shaping\, joining\, and finishing to build a small project. The cours
 e focuses on building foundational skills\, with instructor demonstrations
  and supervised hands-on practice\, to instill confidence and a solid unde
 rstanding for future woodworking projects.\n\nClass runs from 9 a.m. to 5 
 p.m. each day. Class fee is $200 ($180 for Friends of the Museum). Minimum
  age is 16. Course size is limited\, and advance registration is required.
  Register online or by calling 252-504-7758.
