DESCRIPTION:Launching Liberty: The North Carolina Shipbuilding Co. & Its Sh
 ips\npart of the Battleship North Carolina Lecture Series\n\nThe North Car
 olina Shipbuilding Company turned the Cape Fear into a powerhouse of WWII 
 production\, launching 243 vessels between 1941 & 1946.  From Liberty ship
 s to cargo carriers\, these ships carried the people and supplies that kep
 t the Allied war effort moving--and ultimately helped win the war.  \n\nJo
 in John Moseley\, Curator of Education & Outreach\, North Carolina Maritim
 e Museum at Southport\, for a compelling look at the ships\, the shipyard\
 , and the people behind them.  \n\nLecture Ticket: $5  At the Door Ticket:
  $8Friends of the Battleship Members: Free  Lecture begins at 6 pm on Apri
 l 28th.
GEO:34.236158;-77.953643
LOCATION: Battleship North Carolina\, Wardroom
SUMMARY:Launching Liberty: The North Carolina Shipbuilding Co. & Its Ships
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/launching-liberty-the-north-
 carolina-shipbuilding-co-its-ships
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
