DESCRIPTION:You are invited to attend the 20th annual Daniel Boone Festival
  in Mocksville\, North Carolina. Every year\, Davie County puts on this ev
 ent to recognize and honor the infamous pioneer and frontiersman\, who liv
 ed in Davie County from 1756 until 1764.  \n\nThe Davie County Historical 
 and Genealogical Society will sponsor guided tours departing at 10:15 a.m.
 \, 12:15 p.m.\, and 2:15 p.m.\n\nStops include the Historic Joppa Cemetery
 \, where members of the Boone family are buried\, the Boone Tract at Bear 
 Creek\, the Daniel Boone Marker in Farmington\, Pudding Ridge\, and other 
 significant Revolutionary War locations.
GEO:35.909176;-80.578302
LOCATION:Numerous locations throughout Mocksville\, North Carolina.
SUMMARY:20th Annual Daniel Boone Festival 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/20th-annual-daniel-boone-fes
 tival
