DTSTART:20260503T170000Z
DTEND:20260503T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Starting May 1\, Museum mammalogist Dr. Roland Kays and colleag
 ues will retrace the historic route of Lewis and Clark\, comparing histori
 c wildlife observations to what camera traps find today. Along the way\, K
 ays and company will meet local experts to learn how animal populations ha
 ve changed over the 250 years of our country’s history. Follow along on 
 the Return of the Wild website and YouTube channel. You can also join us a
 t the Daily Planet Theater (or on the Museum’s YouTube channel) for live
  check-ins with the team at 1pm on May 3\, 10 and 16 as well as 11am on Ma
 y 28\, June 4 and June 17.
GEO:35.782138;-78.641055
LOCATION:NC Museum of Natural Sciences\, Daily Planet Theater (NRC)
SUMMARY:Return of the Wild: A Lewis & Clark Resurvey
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/return-of-the-wild-a-lewis-c
 lark-resurvey
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
