DESCRIPTION:Iredell County Public Library Commemorates 250 Years of Freedom
  with Year-Long Exhibit Series\n\nThe Iredell County Public Library will h
 ost a series of four local history exhibits throughout 2026 as part of Ame
 rica 250\, the 250th anniversary of the signing of the Declaration of Inde
 pendence. The inaugural exhibit\, Visions of Freedom\, will open to the pu
 blic on January 12 on the Main floor of the Statesville branch library.\n\
 nVisions of Freedom will focus on highlighting local landmarks\, Revolutio
 nary era residents\, and important social movements that not only shaped t
 he nation\, but the Iredell County community. This free exhibit will offer
  a blend of information\, images\, and engaging interactive activities des
 igned to appeal to visitors of all ages.\n\nFor more details about the exh
 ibit series and upcoming local history events\, please visit our website a
 t https://iredell.lib.nc.us or contact Shellie Taylor at michelle.taylor@i
 redellcountync.gov\n\nStatesville Library Hours: M-Th 8am-8pm\, F & Sat 9a
 m-6pm
GEO:35.787463;-80.88791
LOCATION:Iredell County Public Library\, Main level
SUMMARY:Visions of Freedom\, Exhibit #1 (Iredell County Public Library: Mai
 n Branch-Statesville)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/visions-of-freedom-exhibit-1
 -iredell-county-public-library-main-branch-statesville
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
END:VEVENT
