DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260508
DESCRIPTION:Friends of Lower Haw is offering another outing in its “Take 
 a Walk on the Wild Side” hiking series in the Lower Haw River State Natu
 ral Area. We are fortunate to still have some wildness with this amazing n
 atural resource running through a growing urbanized area. Join Outdoor NC 
 Guide & Haw River native Ben Clarke and his trusty dog Rocco for a spectac
 ular 1.5 mile round-trip evening hike down the west bank of the Haw from H
 ighway 64. We'll pass some of the most famous rapids on the river and lots
  of native mountain laurel\, which should be at the peak of their flowerin
 g season! Our hike will take us to Gabriel's Bend\, a Class III rapid wher
 e the Haw has cut a mighty cliff out of the riverbank. The trail climbs th
 is cliff to a unique overlook surveying more than a mile of the river! Ple
 ase be aware that this hike involves plenty of rock scrabbling\, uneven gr
 ound on informal trails\, and the risk of poison ivy\, ticks\, and mosquit
 os. Sturdy shoes\, bug spray\, and water recommended! Friendly dogs on lea
 sh are welcome but may struggle with the terrain. Anyone up for a somewhat
  challenging but highly rewarding hike are welcome - no pre-registration r
 equired! Contact lowerhawevents@gmail.com for questions or to let us know 
 you’re coming.
GEO:35.730547;-79.107059
LOCATION:US 64 Haw River Canoe Access
SUMMARY:Gabriel's Bend Overlook Hike
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/gabriels-bend-overlook-hike
END:VEVENT
