DESCRIPTION:In recognition of the United States’ 250th anniversary\, the 
 Asheville Choral Society presents Out Of Many\, One\, a thoughtful and ric
 hly textured concert exploring the many voices that have shaped the nation
 ’s identity.\n\n\nPerformances will take place May 8 and 9 at Central Un
 ited Methodist Church.\nDrawing inspiration from the phrase E Pluribus Unu
 m—“out of many\, one”—the program\nweaves together a wide range of
  musical traditions\, reflecting the diverse cultural roots\,\nhistories\,
  and perspectives that continue to define the United States. Through folk 
 songs\,\nspirituals\, and contemporary choral works\, the concert invites 
 audiences to consider both the promise of unity and the realities of a sha
 red history that is still unfolding.\nPerformed by a 130-voice chorus know
 n for its professional-level sound\, the program balances moments of celeb
 ration with opportunities for reflection.\n\n\nTraditional melodies sit al
 ongside modern compositions\, offering space to honor resilience\,\nacknow
 ledge struggle\, and recognize the ongoing work of building a more inclusi
 ve and\nequitable society.\n\n\nSelections in the program draw from Indige
 nous\, African American\, Appalachian\, and immigrant musical traditions\,
  as well as works that speak to themes of home\, service\, identity\, and 
 belonging. The result is not a single narrative\, but a musical conversati
 on - one that embraces complexity while pointing toward connection.\n\n\nT
 he concert also features appearances by Tempus\, the Asheville Choral Soci
 ety’s select vocal ensemble\, whose chamber performances add an addition
 al layer of intimacy and nuance to the program.\n\nUnder the direction of 
 Artistic Director and conductor Dr. Melodie Galloway\, the Asheville Chora
 l Society continues to present programs that are both artistically compell
 ing and culturally resonant.\n\n“This program is an opportunity to refle
 ct on who we are\, and who we are still becoming\,” said Dr. Galloway. 
 “The idea of E Pluribus Unum is both an aspiration and a challenge. Thro
 ugh this music\, we honor the many voices that have shaped our shared stor
 y - and we hold space for listening\, for understanding\, and for connecti
 on.”\n\n\nOut Of Many\, One invites audiences into a musical experience 
 that is at once celebratory and contemplative - a reminder that the streng
 th of a chorus\, like that of a nation\, lies not in uniformity\, but in t
 he willingness of many voices to come together.
GEO:35.593125;-82.553545
LOCATION:Central United Methodist Church\, Asheville
SUMMARY:Asheville Choral Society presents Out Of Many\, One
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/asheville-choral-society-pre
 sents-out-of-many-one
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
END:VEVENT
