DESCRIPTION:Join the Library of NC’s Government and Heritage Library and 
 the State Archives of NC for a Community Scanning Day! Bring your family p
 hotographs\, letters\, and historical documents to be digitized for free w
 ith assistance from library and archives staff. This is a great opportunit
 y to preserve your family history and contribute to North Carolina’s sha
 red heritage\, and all participants will go home with a free USB drive con
 taining scanned family records.\n\nAdvance registration is required to res
 erve a 15-minute appointment slot between 9:00 AM and 1:00 PM. Each partic
 ipant may bring up to 5 items per appointment\, and items must be no large
 r than standard letter size (8.5" x 11"). During the appointment\, our tea
 m will scan your materials for you and provide guidance on caring for your
  originals and digital files\, and you’ll also learn about resources for
  genealogy and local history research. Please note that bound or oversized
  materials cannot be scanned at these digitization stations. If you have b
 ound or larger items\, GHL has a self-service BookScanner capable of scann
 ing bound materials and large items\, such as scrapbooks and family bibles
 .\n\nThe event is free and open to the public. Registration is required to
  reserve a 15-minute appointment at a digitization station\; walk-ins are 
 welcome to use the Government and Heritage Library’s self-service BookSc
 anner. To make changes to your appointment time\, please contact us at sln
 c.info@dncr.nc.gov. Register at slnc.info/scanningday.
GEO:35.78292;-78.637155
LOCATION:NC Department of Natural and Cultural Resources\, Library of NC's 
 Government and Heritage Library Reading Room
SUMMARY:Community Scanning Day
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-scanning-day
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
