DESCRIPTION:The introductory wooden boatbuilding class provides hands-on ex
 perience with fundamental boatbuilding concepts. The course teaches studen
 ts to select wood\, design a boat\, and use various techniques like steam 
 bending\, planking (carvel or lapstrake)\, and fastening to construct a sm
 all boat. The curriculum covers basic design\, essential tools\, safe work
 shop practices\, and the properties of wood\, culminating in a small proje
 ct that builds confidence for independent boatbuilding.\n\nClass runs from
  9 a.m. to 5 p.m. each day. Class fee is $200 ($180 for Friends of the Mus
 eum). Minimum age is 16. Course size is limited\, and advance registration
  is required. Register online or by calling 252-504-7758.
GEO:34.717841;-76.666223
LOCATION:North Carolina Maritime Museum in Beaufort
SUMMARY:Introduction to Wooden Boatbuilding
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/introduction-to-wooden-boatb
 uilding-7241
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
