DESCRIPTION:As the nation celebrates 250 years of American independence\, t
 he 2026 show will aim to honor our heritage with a powerful display of air
 power\, patriotic unity\, and national pride.\n\n“The MCAS Cherry Point 
 Air Show is more than an aviation event\, it’s a celebration of American
  excellence and a tribute to the strength\, innovation\, and freedom our n
 ation has stood for over two and a half centuries\,” said Col. Brendan 
 “Cletus” Burks\, commanding officer of MCAS Cherry Point. “In partne
 rship with 2nd Marine Aircraft Wing and our community\, we are proud to ho
 st a world-class event that reflects the professionalism of our Marines an
 d the enduring bond we share with Eastern North Carolina.”\n\nHeadlining
  the 2026 event is the return of the legendary U.S. Navy Blue Angels\, joi
 ned by an exciting lineup of military and civilian acts that continue to i
 nspire and captivate. Fan-favorite performances such as the jet truck\, pa
 rachute jump team\, and aerobatic pilots like Randy Ball\, RJ Gritter and 
 Tom Larkin are already slated to return.\n\nAs always\, the air show will 
 be free and open to the public\, with general admission and parking offere
 d at no cost. Premium seating options will also be available for those see
 king upgraded amenities. Visitors can expect an immersive experience fille
 d with aerial demonstrations\, aircraft static displays\, food vendors\, a
 nd interactive exhibits for guests of all ages.
GEO:34.883197;-76.905866
LOCATION:Marine Corps Air Station Cherry Point
SUMMARY:Cherry Point Air Show
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/cherry-point-air-show
