DESCRIPTION:On the cusp of World War II\, professional artists were commiss
 ioned to design artwork for religious services on military installations\,
  Naval ships\, and in the field. The Citizens Committee for the Army and N
 avy answered the call from Chaplains to provide religious symbolic beauty 
 for their divine services. The result was an extensive program to provide 
 3-piece altar paintings or triptychs. The first one was created for the US
 S North Carolina and lives in the Battleship’s collections. Join us to e
 xplore the art\, history\, and spiritual support for all during World War 
 II.\n\nMay 13\, 2026 at 6 PM\nWardroom\, Battleship North Carolina\n1 Batt
 leship Road\, Wilmington\, NC\n\n$5 in advance\; $8 at the door (as space 
 allows)\nFriends Members: Free\n\nTo purchase tickets\, visit bit.ly/launc
 hingliberty
GEO:34.236158;-77.953643
LOCATION: Battleship North Carolina\, Wardroom
SUMMARY:Triptychs for Victory: Altar Paintings for the American Armed Force
 s in World War II
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/triptychs-for-victory-altar-
 paintings-for-the-american-armed-forces-in-world-war-ii
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
