DTEND:20260516T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Help us kick off our Plott Hound Book Club with a metal stampin
 g bookmark-making workshop and book swap! Grab your previously read books 
 and head to Adventures in Bloom in downtown Apex for a one-of-a-kind exper
 ience. Your ticket grants you access to both the bookmark workshop and the
  book swap. After crafting your own metal-stamped bookmark\, hang out with
  other PHLC readers and pick up any of the books that catch your eye in th
 e swap! Not a PHLC book club member? That’s OK—join us anyway! Beverag
 es and snacks are BYOB. \n\nPlease note: Due to space restrictions\, visit
 ors in groups should buy multiple tickets simultaneously to guarantee seat
 s together.\n\nFree parking is available behind the building next to the t
 rain tracks on a first-come\, first-served basis. To learn more about Adve
 ntures in Bloom\, visit their website.
GEO:35.731159;-78.851153
LOCATION:Adventures in Bloom
SUMMARY:Metal Stamping Bookmark Workshop and Book Swap
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/metal-stamping-bookmark-work
 shop-and-book-swap
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042638Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52709773555586
DTSTART:20260516T140000Z
DTEND:20260516T183000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for “Mountain Mothers\,” a special guided tour at V
 ance Birthplace that looks closely at the experiences of mothers and child
 ren in 19th-century Western North Carolina.\n\nExplore the spaces where wo
 men like Mira Vance\, Leah Erwin\, and Elizabeth Hemphill would have had t
 o navigate pregnancy and childbirth as we discuss maternal health and fami
 ly dynamics in Southern Appalachia in the 1800s. This tour will cover both
  the joys and the dangers of childbearing in an environment shaped by slav
 ery and war and with limited access to medical resources. Due to the sensi
 tive and difficult nature of some of the topics we will explore\, we recom
 mend this tour for mature audiences only. \n\nRegister via Zeffy to reserv
 e your spot! Tours are offered at 10am and 1pm and will run for approximat
 ely 75 minutes. Tickets are free for mothers and $5 each otherwise. Spaces
  are limited\, so claim your spot today! \n\nThis special program is spons
 ored by the Mountain History and Culture Group. All proceeds go towards su
 pplies and materials for educational programming at Vance Birthplace.
GEO:35.700986;-82.496251
LOCATION:Governor Zebulon B. Vance Birthplace
SUMMARY:Mountain Mothers: A Special Guided Tour at Vance Birthplace
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mountain-mothers-a-special-g
 uided-tour-at-vance-birthplace
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Guided Tours
CATEGORIES:Special Site Programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042638Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52648811154855
DTSTART:20260516T140000Z
DTEND:20260516T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Rootle Roadster Tour will be making a stop at the Potato Fe
 stival on Saturday\, May 16\, from 10 a.m. to 2 p.m. The Museum of the Alb
 emarle\, a part of the Division of State History Museums\, Office of Archi
 ves and History\, is an agency of the North Carolina Department of Natural
  and Cultural Resources.\n\nFamilies with children ages 8 and younger will
  receive free\, playful learning experiences in their community. The event
  will feature hands-on activities\, educational resources\, and demonstrat
 ions by community partners. All activities and takeaways are aligned with 
 literacy\, physical\, sensory\, social-emotional\, and STEM curriculum. \n
 \nThe Rootle Roadster Tour is made possible through the Albemarle Alliance
  for Children and Families.
GEO:36.296532;-76.219757
LOCATION:Museum of the Albemarle
SUMMARY:Rootle Roadster Tour
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/rootle-roadster-tour
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Youth & Family Activities
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042638Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207082963176
DTSTART:20260516T140000Z
DTEND:20260516T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for sur
 vival\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fight
 s back in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the 
 world with unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with tr
 ippy toads\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover h
 ow these defenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage an
 d mimicry\, specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink
  bombs\, caboose cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, st
 and their ground or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live ani
 mal encounters\, larger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and 
 interactive programs.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of al
 l ages. Offered in English & Spanish.
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042638Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51878259898661
DTSTART:20260516T140000Z
DTEND:20260516T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:KMHM is excited to present Women at the Edge of War: Carolina P
 iedmont's Heroines of the American Revolution. This exhibit highlights the
  daily courage and civic work of women in the Carolinas\, whose efforts we
 re essential to Revolutionary resistance and survival on the southern fron
 tier.\n\nThe exhibit will run from Feb. 17\, 2026 to May 30\, 2026. The mu
 seum is open Tues-Sat\, 10-4. Admission is free. Check out kingsmountainmu
 seum.org or call 704-739-1019 for more information.
GEO:35.239004;-81.342181
LOCATION:Kings Mountain Historical Museum
SUMMARY:Women at the Edge of War: Carolina Piedmont's Heroines of the Ameri
 can Revolution
