DESCRIPTION:In May 1771\, an armed band of backcountry farmers known as the
  Regulators clashed with Royal Governor William Tryon’s North Carolina m
 ilitia on the very ground now preserved as the Alamance Battleground State
  Historic Site. \n\nThis spring\, join us as we honor the 255th anniversar
 y with a special reenactment and commemoration. Mark your calendars and st
 ay tuned for details on how you can experience history brought vividly to 
 life.
GEO:36.009795;-79.521351
LOCATION:Alamance Battleground State Historic Site
