DESCRIPTION:Back by popular demand! Join the Old Salem metalworkers to crea
 te your own pewter spoon. Pewter was a common material for dining ware in 
 the 18th century and along with tin smithing\, made up a large portion of 
 the metalwork occurring in early Salem.\n\nCome participate in the magic o
 f casting and learn the skills of finishing fine pewterware\, just like th
 e pewterers of Salem in the 1700’s. Participants will use traditional to
 ols and methods to create their own keepsake pewter spoon to take home!\n\
 nSpace is limited to eight (8) participants. Workshop is appropriate for a
 ges 16+ (participants under 18 must be accompanied by a ticketed adult).
GEO:36.087337;-80.242156
LOCATION:Old Salem Museums & Gardens\, Single Brothers House
SUMMARY:Pewter Spoon Making at Old Salem
