UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52560463473947
DTSTART:20260517T190000Z
DTEND:20260517T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Come\, be a part of history!\nThe Psalm of Joy will be presente
 d at the Raleigh Moravian Church\, May 17\, 2026 at 3:00pm. The concert/se
 rvice of music and word is free. An informative talk will precede the conc
 ert at 1:30pm with a band prelude at 2:30pm. Psalm of Joy is an ode (a ser
 vice of word and music) created by Moravian composer Johann Friedrich Pete
 r (1746–1813) and performed on July 4\, 1783\, as part of the first orga
 nized July 4th celebration in the nation. \nThis year we are celebrating t
 he 250th anniversary of the signing of the Declaration of Independence. Af
 ter years of suffering and turmoil\, the end of the Revolutionary War foun
 d the Moravians citizens of a brand-new nation. When the Moravians in Nort
 h Carolina received a letter from Governor Alexander Martin (ca. 1739–18
 07) proclaiming July 4th a day of celebration and thanksgiving\, the Morav
 ians turned (as they always do) to music. Rather than revel in victory\; h
 owever\, it was the return of peace that spoke to them and inspired the mu
 sic of this joyful work. Whether it is in regard to the end of armed confl
 icts or a respite from the chaos of everyday life\, this message of gratit
 ude\, peace\, and joy endures.\nTalk: History of the Psalm of Joy\, Sunday
  1:30pm\nMoravian Band Prelude\, 2:30pm\nConcert / Service – Sunday 3:00
 pm (about 50 minutes)\nWant to learn the music and participate in the choi
 r or the band? All are welcome on Saturday\, May 16. Please find all the d
 etails and register at https://moravianmusic.org/psalm-of-joy-raleigh/
GEO:35.813378;-78.68264
LOCATION:Raleigh Moravian Church\, sanctuary
SUMMARY:Psalm of Joy
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/psalm-of-joy
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
CATEGORIES:Concerts (Music)
END:VEVENT
