UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52463262601204
DTSTART:20260517T213000Z
DTEND:20260517T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:May is nationally recognized as a time to focus on mental healt
 h and well-being. To explore the powerful connection between healing and a
 rt\, join us for an evening with seven-time Grammy-nominated performing ar
 tist Nnenna Freelon.\n\nThroughout this evening author event\, Freelon gui
 des the audience through an intimate blend of music\, spoken word\, and st
 orytelling that reflects on love\, loss\, and the creative process. The pr
 ogram connects to her latest book\, Beneath the Skin of Sorrow: Improvisat
 ions on Loss\, which invites readers into a thoughtful conversation about 
 how grief and creativity intersect\, drawing from the rich traditions of B
 lack heritage and the expressive language of jazz.\n\nTicket purchase incl
 udes access to the event. Refreshments will be available for purchase duri
 ng the show. Attendees will also enjoy special pricing and author signing 
 of the book Beneath the Skin of Sorrow: Improvisations on Loss.\n\nPlease 
 enter through the front doors of West Building.
GEO:35.807856;-78.703922
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art
SUMMARY:She Sings\, She Speaks: Beneath the Skin with Nnenna Freelon
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/she-sings-she-speaks-beneath
 -the-skin-with-nnenna-freelon
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
CATEGORIES:Concerts (Music)
END:VEVENT
