DTEND:20260519T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:The waters off Cape Fear hold the world’s largest concentrati
 on of American Civil War shipwrecks. Between 1861 and 1865\, the Union Nav
 y sought to blockade the Confederate port of Wilmington\, North Carolina\,
  resulting in the loss of nearly 33 vessels along\nthe coast and waterways
  of the Lower Cape Fear.\n\nJoin Stephen Atkinson\, MA\, RPA\, Deputy Stat
 e Archaeologist – Underwater\, for an exploration of blockade running ac
 tivity in the Wilmington area. Drawing on the North Carolina Underwater Ar
 chaeology Branch’s ongoing archaeological monitoring efforts\, Atkinson 
 will examine notable wrecks while sharing stories and insights about the m
 any vessels lost in the shadow of Fort Fisher.\n\nTuesday\, May 19\, 2026 
 | 6:00 PM\nBattleship North Carolina Wardroom\n1 Battleship Road\, Wilming
 ton\, NC\n\nAdmission:\n$5 advance online registration\n$8 at the door\nFr
 iends Members: Free\nSpace is limited! To reserve your spot\, visit bit.ly
 /shadow-of-goliath
GEO:34.236158;-77.953643
LOCATION: Battleship North Carolina\, Wardroom
SUMMARY:In the Shadow of Goliath: Blockade Runners of the Lower Cape Fear
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/in-the-shadow-of-goliath-blo
 ckade-runners-of-the-lower-cape-fear
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Special Site Programs
