DESCRIPTION:Join a Ranger to hike 3 miles round trip to the site of a cemet
 ery of enslaved people. We will discuss laws and statistics related to the
  practice of slavery in NC. This hike does feature discussions about racia
 l violence and content that is more suited to a mature audience. Please at
 tend with a respectful attitude and be prepared for a significant creek cr
 ossing and some short sections of off-trail hiking.\n\nPlease be sure to d
 ress appropriately for the weather\, wear hiking shoes\, and bring water!\
 n\nSpaces are limited\, and registration is required. To sign up\, call (9
 84) 250-1370 or email eno.river@ncparks.gov. Include the number of guests 
 in your party and a phone number where you can be reached if the event is 
 changed or canceled.
GEO:36.078519;-79.005129
LOCATION:Eno River State Park - Fews Ford Access\, Loop Parking Lot (End of
  the Road)
SUMMARY:Untitled Hike
