BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042638Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52816255483582
DTSTART:20260521T220000Z
DTEND:20260521T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:Author Talk: Marcia Phillips — The Regulator Movement in Nort
 h Carolina\nFree Admission\n\nJoin historian\, author\, and preservationis
 t Marcia Phillips for an engaging exploration of North Carolina’s overlo
 oked early freedom fighters—the Regulators. In this compelling talk\, Ph
 illips uncovers how backcountry settlers in the 1760s and early 1770s rose
  up against corrupt colonial leadership\, unjust taxation\, and an unequal
  legal system—years before the outbreak of the American Revolution.\n\nW
 hile much of the Revolution’s story centers on cities like Boston and Ph
 iladelphia\, this program highlights the critical role of the southern col
 onies and the Carolinian frontier. Through vivid storytelling and historic
 al insight\, Phillips connects the Regulator movement to the broader strug
 gle for independence\, showing how it helped shape revolutionary thought\,
  deepen divisions between Loyalists and Patriots\, and influence the South
 ern Campaign of the Revolutionary War.\n\nThis program offers a deeper und
 erstanding of how the fight for American liberty began not only in the Nor
 th\, but in the hills and backcountry of pre-Revolutionary North Carolina.
 \n\nA book sale and signing will follow the presentation. Refreshments wil
 l be provided.\n\nDate & Time: Thursday\, May 21\, 6:00 PM\nLocation: Gene
 alogy & Local History Room\nLexington Public Library\n612 S. Main Street\,
  Lexington\, NC 27292\n\nCo-hosted by the Davidson County Historical Museu
 m and the Lexington Public Library Genealogy & Local History Room.
GEO:35.819216;-80.260352
LOCATION:Lexington Public Library\, Genealogy & Local History Room
SUMMARY:Author Talk: Marcia Phillips - The Regulator Movement in North Caro
 lina
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/author-talk-marcia-phillips-
 the-regulator-movement-in-north-carolina
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
