DESCRIPTION:Join Historic Edenton State Historic Site on Saturday\, May 23\
 , for an ancestry research seminar focused on the challenges in researchin
 g African American heritage\, tips for specialty research\, and finding Re
 volutionary War ancestors. This event\, located at the Historic 1767 Chowa
 n County Courthouse\, brings together genealogy experts to share proven st
 rategies\, specialized tools\, and practical tips for tracing family roots
 . Guarantee your seat at this unique event by pre-registration call the Hi
 storic Edenton Visitor Center at (252) 632-5200 to register. \n\nSchedule:
 \n\n9:00 - Doors open for registration\n\n9:50 - Welcome and introduction 
 of committee members\n\n10:00 - 10:45 - Taryn Kennedy - African American R
 evolutionary War Patriots in Family Trees\n\n11:00 - 11:45 - Shannon Combs
 -Bennet - Finding Your Family Using DNA Technology\n\n12:00 - 1:00 - Lunch
 \n\n1:00 - 1:45 - Dr. Mark Attucks\, Sr. - First to Defy - First to Die: T
 he Attucks Legacy\n\n2:00 - 2:45 - Finding Your Story - workshop session w
 ith the speakers
GEO:36.061713;-76.607716
LOCATION:Historic Edenton\, 1767 Chowan County Courthouse
SUMMARY:We Were There Too: Searching For Ancestors
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/we-were-there-too-searching-
 for-ancestors
