DESCRIPTION:RESCHEDULED - This event has been rescheduled from May 7th to M
 ay 29th\, 10 am-1 pm due to rainy weather. Please re-register using the sa
 me link to reserve your spot.\n\nFriends of the Blue Ridge invites outdoor
  enthusiasts to a unique hiking adventure\, “Elk Knob Trails Past and Fu
 ture\,” at Elk Knob State Park on Wednesday\, May 7th. This guided excur
 sion will be led by NC State Park Ranger Marissa Mabe. As participants tre
 k to the summit\, Ranger Mabe will share the rich history of the park and 
 the surrounding mountains. Hikers will also learn to identify the flora an
 d fauna that call the Elk Knob area home\, highlighting the ecological sig
 nificance of this high-elevation landscape. In addition to exploring exist
 ing paths\, the event will feature an educational discussion regarding the
  future of the park’s trail system. Highlights include an introduction t
 o the Northern Peaks Trail\, an ambitious project that will eventually con
 nect downtown Boone to West Jefferson by crossing the Amphibolite Mountain
 s.\n\nTo ensure an intimate and educational experience\, the group size is
  strictly limited to 15\nparticipants. To secure a spot\, visit www.blueri
 dgefriends.org/hcregistration\n\nAbout Friends of the Blue Ridge:\nFriends
  of the Blue Ridge is a non-profit organization dedicated to preserving th
 e cultural and\nnatural resources of the Blue Ridge region through communi
 ty engagement and volunteerism.\n\nParticipants MUST register for this pro
 gram.
GEO:36.333462;-81.696432
LOCATION:Elk Knob State Park
SUMMARY:Elk Knob Trails: Past and Future
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/elk-knob-trails-past-and-fut
 ure
