DESCRIPTION:Homeschool Day is back at the Charlotte Museum of History! Join
  us for a special day designed just for homeschool families\, with hands-o
 n activities\, crafts\, and interactive experiences that bring Charlotte
 ’s history to life.\n\nThroughout the historic homesite\, families can e
 xplore a variety of activity tables created especially for students in gra
 des 3–6. Young historians can try their hand at:\n\nTextile production b
 y making a mini loom and learning how to weave\n\nWater filtration at the 
 historic Springhouse by building a filter using natural materials\n\nQuill
  and ink writing and discover how important documents in our nation’s hi
 story were created\n\nPrinting and the printing press by making a stamp an
 d creating a print of their own\n\nRevolutionary War spy communication by 
 writing with invisible ink and decoding messages using the Culper Spy Ring
  Code\n\n…and more!\n\nFamilies will also have the opportunity to explor
 e our newest exhibit\, The American Revolution: The Augmented Exhibition\,
  an immersive and interactive experience that uses HistoPads to bring Revo
 lutionary War stories to life through augmented reality. This exhibit is e
 specially great for middle and high school students\, but younger learners
  will enjoy it too. To help students engage at their own level\, we’ll h
 ave companion activity booklets for elementary\, middle\, and high school 
 ages available while they explore.\n\nWhether your students love hands-on 
 learning\, local history\, or interactive technology\, Homeschool Day offe
 rs something for the whole family!
GEO:35.23394;-80.766646
LOCATION:Charlotte Museum of History
SUMMARY:Homeschool Day 2026
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/homeschool-day-2026
