DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special program that explores Black military hist
 ory through Black GI Joe action figures. Free with admission to the doll\,
  toy & miniature museum! 2 timeslots.\n\nEnjoy an all-ages PowerPoint pres
 entation from presenter Les Albers\, a military veteran\, historical inter
 preter\, and re-enactor.\n\nLes will use a display of thirteen 12-inch GI 
 Joe figures to trace the Black military experience from 1778 through 2003.
 \nEach GI Joe figure represents a chapter in American history.\n\nYou’ll
  learn the names and stories of real Black servicemen and servicewomen\, t
 he military conflicts in which they served\, and the evolution of military
  uniforms across multiple centuries.\n\nYou’ll also learn the historical
  significance of Black GI Joe figures with a spotlight on their developmen
 t between 1965 and 1997.\n\nAppropriate for all ages. Offered in-person on
 ly (though we hope to replicate as an online experience in the future!)\n\
 nDate & Location:\nSaturday\, May 30\, 2026\n2 timeslots. The same program
  will be presented in each timeslot:\n11 am to 11:40 am\n1 pm to 1:40 pm\n
 \nAt the NC Museum of Dolls\, Toys & Miniatures at 440 South Salisbury Ave
 nue\, Spencer\, NC 28159\n\nCost & Registration:\nFREE with museum admissi
 on. No registration is required. Just pay admission to the museum at the d
 oor when you arrive (cash or card).\nAdmission ranges from $5 to $10 per p
 erson.\nAdmission to our museum is always free for museum members\, so con
 sider becoming a museum member! It’s a huge source of annual support to 
 our nonprofit!
GEO:35.68939;-80.43524
LOCATION:N.C. Museum of Dolls\, Toys & Miniatures
SUMMARY:Learning Black Military History with GI Joes
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/learning-black-military-hist
 ory-with-gi-joes
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
END:VEVENT
