UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52639419877219
DTSTART:20260531T180000Z
DTEND:20260531T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Dive into the stories and drama behind The American Constitutio
 n film & the unsung delegates who crafted a document that changed the worl
 d! This event is free of charge and the director\, David Garrigus\, will b
 e on hand to answer questions after the showing.\n\nExperience the groundb
 reaking film that unveils the Constitution's dramatic creation. Set in 178
 7 Philadelphia\, "The American Constitution" features a stellar cast of ac
 tors who bring the framers to life. Best-selling authors and leading histo
 rians masterfully reveal how George Washington\, James Madison\, Alexander
  Hamilton\, Benjamin Franklin and a cadre of unsung delegates crafted a do
 cument that changed the world. The filmmaker\, David Garrigus\, the award-
 winning filmmaker behind the PBS critically-acclaimed " Kitty Hawk\; The W
 right Brothers' Journey of Invention\," will be on hand to engage in discu
 ssion and questions.\n\nDr. Harry Watson\, retired history professor\, UNC
 -Chapel Hill\, will speak to North Carolina's role in signing the Constitu
 tion before the film.\n\nComplimentary refreshments will be served after t
 he screening by the Moyock Woman's Club.
GEO:36.374283;-75.965499
LOCATION:Currituck County Middle School\, Auditorium
SUMMARY:The American Constitution Documentary Film Showing
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/the-american-constitution-do
 cumentary-film-showing
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
END:VEVENT
