UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52931662545346
DTSTART:20260601T223000Z
DTEND:20260602T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Discussing Home to Harlem by Claude McKay | Monday\, June 1st\,
  6:30pm at Main Library in Hillsborough | As part of Orange County Public 
 Library's Black Literature\, Arts\, & Culture Festival (BLAC Fest)\, First
  Monday Classics Book Club and local author\, James Maxey is discussing Ho
 me to Harlem by Black\, queer author\, Claude McKay. The work gives voice 
 to the alienation of Black people in 1920's Harlem when it became a fashio
 nable place to live. The full text of the book is available free online in
  a number of places including Hathi Trust. Click here to view or download 
 Home to Harlem.  Click here for additional BLAC Fest event information.
GEO:36.074254;-79.100646
LOCATION:Orange County Public Library - Main Library
SUMMARY:Discussing "Home to Harlem" by Claude McKay with Local Author\, Jam
 es Maxey
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/discussing-home-to-harlem-by
 -claude-mckay-with-local-author-james-maxey
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Panels & Book Discussions
END:VEVENT
