BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042639Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52895316668889
DTSTART:20260602T170000Z
DTEND:20260602T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a webinar on June 2\, 2026\, from 1:00 to 2:00 PM w
 ith North Carolina author and educator Carol Baldwin\, who will discuss ho
 w to research and write historical fiction.\n\nCarol will share insights f
 rom the research process while writing her young adult novel Half-Truths\,
  a work of historical fiction set in 1950s North Carolina. In this webinar
 \, participants will learn how to locate sources to research the past. Par
 ticipants will also learn practical approaches to conducting historical re
 search and gain insight into how historical inquiry supports narrative sto
 rytelling.\n\nA live Q&A session will follow the presentation\, and attend
 ees will have the opportunity to\nengage directly with the author. Registr
 ation is required. This event will be recorded and made available to the p
 ublic through the Library of NC YouTube channel. Register at slnc.info/bal
 dwin226. This event is free and open to the public.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Researching and Writing Historical Fiction Webinar
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/researching-and-writing-hist
 orical-fiction-webinar
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042639Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52922631966490
DTSTART:20260602T210000Z
DTEND:20260602T223000Z
DESCRIPTION:Love a good mystery? Join us for immersive escape-style games f
 eaturing unique themes throughout the year. The FBI needs your team of leg
 endary treasure hunters to recover a stolen magical lamp hidden behind Roo
 sevelt’s secret clue trail before the mysterious Red Hand can use its po
 wer against democracy. Solve puzzles\, recover the missing Templar locks\,
  and secure the lamp in this National Treasure-inspired escape adventure f
 illed with American symbols\, hidden secrets\, and high-stakes mystery. Re
 gistration Required
GEO:33.922523;-78.578901
LOCATION:Southwest Brunswick Branch Library\, 127
SUMMARY:Booked for Murder and Mayhem: National Treasure Escape with Aladdin
 's Lamp
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/booked-for-murder-and-mayhem
 -national-treasure-escape-with-aladdins-lamp
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Youth & Family Activities
END:VEVENT
