DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260612
DESCRIPTION:Attention Educators! NC History Day invites you to apply for Na
 tional History Day® (NHD) latest iteration of its Historical Argumentatio
 n: Using Library of Congress Resources to Build a Historical Argument\, Ex
 ploring Innovation: Impact\, Influence\, Change in History webinar series.
  \n\nSponsored by the Library of Congress\, this online professional devel
 opment series is designed to deepen participants’ understanding of histo
 rical argumentation and to provide educators with resources and strategies
  for their classrooms. The webinar series will run from late July 2026 to 
 November 2026 and educators may earn 90 professional development hours or 
 three graduate extension credits at no cost.\n\nThroughout this series\, e
 ducators will build their knowledge of teaching with online Library of Con
 gress resources\, complete assignments\, and join monthly webinars. Once c
 omplete\, educators will have demonstrated the ability to share key strate
 gies for researching\, supporting\, and presenting historical arguments bo
 lstered by primary sources held by the Library of Congress. Apply here by 
 June 12th.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Teaching Historical Argumentation Webinar Series: Using Library of 
 Congress Resources to Build a Historical Argument\, Exploring Innovation: 
 Impact\, Influence\, Change in History 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/teacher-historical-argumenta
 tion-webinar-series-using-library-of-congress-resources-to-build-a-histori
 cal-argument-exploring-innovation-impact-influence-change-in-history
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
