DESCRIPTION:Discover North Carolina’s rich African American heritage thro
 ugh a showcase of cultural and historic sites across the state. Explore po
 werful stories of resilience\, achievement\, and community found in landma
 rks throughout North Carolina. Join us as the NC African American Heritage
  Commission uncovers the past that shapes our present.\n\nBio:\nNatalie Ro
 driguez is the Associate Director for the North Carolina African American 
 Heritage Commission (NCAAHC). She earned her bachelor's degree in history 
 from the HBCU NC Central University and her master’s degree in Public Hi
 story from NC State University. In addition to working with organizations 
 such as the National Park Service and North Carolina Historic Sites\, she 
 has also served as the Tour Coordinator at the North Carolina State Capito
 l for a number of years. She enjoys using her passion for public history a
 s a tool to promote\, protect\, and preserve North Carolina’s history fo
 r all people.
GEO:35.67247;-80.932577
LOCATION:Lake Norman State Park
SUMMARY:NC Emancipation Stories
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/nc-emancipation-stories-3526
