BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042640Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52947612431811
DTSTART:20260619T210000Z
DTEND:20260620T030000Z
DESCRIPTION:Honor history and celebrate a visionary future at the 5th Annua
 l Juneteenth Jubilee in downtown Fayetteville. This powerful community cel
 ebration commemorates the end of enslavement in the United States while hi
 ghlighting the profound contributions of Black Americans to the broad tape
 stry of arts\, culture\, and history.\n\nThe 2026 jubilee centers on the t
 heme of Afrofuturism\, creating a vibrant space where historical achieveme
 nts meet a forward-looking vision of innovation and progress. Visitors can
  experience a thoughtfully curated lineup of live entertainment\, soulful 
 music\, and engaging art installations that connect the threads of the Bla
 ck American experience from the past to the present and beyond.\n\nDesigne
 d to be as educational as it is entertaining\, the festival promotes a spi
 rit of unity for all ages. Whether you are exploring the interactive exhib
 its or enjoying the local food and market vendors\, the jubilee offers a w
 elcoming atmosphere that invites both reflection and joy.\n\nCheck the web
 site for a full schedule of performers and guest speakers.
