DESCRIPTION:"A man's rights rest in three boxes. The ballot box\, jury box 
 and the cartridge box. Let no man be kept from the ballot box because of h
 is color. Let no woman be kept from the ballot box..." -Frederick Douglass
 \, November 15th\, 1867.\n\n\nJoin us in June for an exploration of voting
