DTEND:20260624T143000Z
DESCRIPTION:Looking around\, you’ll notice rocks are different from one a
 nother\, but did you know rocks have different classifications or grouping
 s? Would you like to learn how to group like rocks together and discover w
 hat makes rocks different from one another? Join a Ranger for an interacti
 ve activity about\, you guessed it\, rocks!\n\nAll children must be accomp
 anied by an adult. Please be sure to dress appropriately for the weather\,
  wear hiking shoes\, and bring water!\n\nSpaces are limited\, and registra
 tion is required. To sign up\, call (984) 250-1370 or email eno.river@ncpa
 rks.gov. Include the number of guests in your party and a phone number whe
 re you can be reached if the event is changed or canceled.
GEO:36.078519;-79.005129
LOCATION:Eno River State Park - Fews Ford Access\, Visitor Center Classroom
  (Third Right)
SUMMARY:Basics of Rock Identification
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/basics-of-rock-identificatio
 n-5653
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Youth & Family Activities
END:VEVENT
