 ork Parking Area (milepost 299.9 on the Blue Ridge Parkway) for a wildflow
 er and pollinator ID hike along the Upper Boone Fork Trail. Learn how to I
 D some common blooming wildflower species of the high country\, and some l
 ocal pollinator species that keep those flowers blooming every year. \n\nT
 his 1.5 mile easy hike does have some tree roots and rocks to walk over\, 
 so please wear appropriate hiking shoes and dress for the weather.\n\nTher
 e are no bathrooms at Boone Fork Parking Area.
