UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52806721155441
DTSTART:20260715T160000Z
DTEND:20260715T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Andrew Duppstadt\, education and interpretation supervisor for 
 the North Carolina Division of State Historic Sites\, will highlight some 
 of North Carolina’s most famous (or infamous) seafaring personalities\, 
 pirates\, privateers\, and commerce raiders. The presentation explores ove
 r 150 years of maritime history\, including Sir Walter Raleigh\, the Golde
 n Age of Piracy\, the American Revolution\, the War of 1812\, and the Amer
 ican Civil War.
GEO:36.296532;-76.219757
LOCATION:Museum of the Albemarle\, Gaither Auditorium
SUMMARY:History for Lunch: “A Highly Planned and Cooperative Form of Thef
 t:” North Carolina’s Naval Raiders\, 1700–1865
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-for-lunch-a-highly-p
 lanned-and-cooperative-form-of-theft-north-carolinas-naval-raiders-1700186
 5
