BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042641Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51815547918503
DTSTART:20260715T170000Z
DTEND:20260715T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we hike down to Otter Falls (1.2 miles round trip) t
 o learn about how living and non-living things interact in mountain stream
 s. What are all of those insects and other critters swimming and crawling 
 through the creek? We will catch and identify what type of creature they a
 re and what these species could tell us about water quality. Nets will be 
 provided. Any participants wanting to get into the stream should bring clo
 thes and shoes that can get wet and a towel to dry off. Make sure to bring
  water for the hike! No pets please. This is a Ranger Workshop with The To
 wn of Seven Devils.
GEO:36.149669;-81.808644
LOCATION:Otter Falls Trail
SUMMARY:Ranger Workshop - Stream Ecology
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ranger-workshop-stream-ecolo
 gy
