DESCRIPTION:Thomas Day State Historic Site invites K-12 educators to join u
 s for a half-day professional development workshop that explores the roles
  of local history and primary sources in shaping meaningful instruction\, 
 with a focused look at Caswell County's school desegregation story.\n\nThr
 ough a blend of hands-on research and discussion\, participants will learn
  how to discover\, analyze\, and teach with local primary sources to help 
 students connect national history to their own communities. This session i
 s completely free of charge\, and catered lunch is provided at no addition
 al cost. Participants may receive .45 CEU credits. \n\nWhile the workshop 
 is designed for K-12 classroom teachers\, educators (current or former) of
  any kind are encouraged to register. \n\nPlease complete the form to regi
 ster: https://forms.gle/eLbAryWhQym3vpig7
GEO:36.538687;-79.20624
LOCATION:Thomas Day State Historic Site
SUMMARY:Teacher Workshop: Exploring Caswell County's School Desegregation H
 istory Through Primary Sources
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/teacher-workshop-exploring-c
 aswell-countys-school-desegregation-history-through-primary-sources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
