BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042642Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52258839949760
DTSTART:20260725T140000Z
DTEND:20260725T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Learn about the lives of sailors who will become a part of our 
 new nation’s defense and what a local seaport was like as they prepared 
 for war. \n\nSpeak with the ships’ surgeons and sailors who are awaiting
  the next boat to depart. Drop by the Tavern for talk of the simmering war
  and outrage over British impressment of sailors. See musket firings demon
 strations as the men prepare for war.\n\nBook signing and talk by Benjamin
  Schaffer on The First Fleets: Colonial Navies of the British Atlantic Wor
 ld\, a new book revealing the little-known and misunderstood provincial na
 vies established by North American British colonists.Join us as we host th
 ese costumed reenactors and guides to tell our story:\n\nNaval Living Hist
 ory reenactors representing the colonial navies of Virginia\, North Caroli
 na\, and South Carolina on sailmaking\, navigation\, sailor’s life\, and
  open fire cookingShip’s surgeonsScrimshaw demonstrationColonial townspe
 ople with children’s games Boatman using pitch to caulk a boat hull  Rop
 emaking Ship’s carpentrySpinning and weaving America 250th airstreamGene
 alogists with local information and on the seaman’s legacy group: Order 
 of the Sea and Sail St Thomas Church with guides Munitions demonstrations 
 at Bonner’s Point throughout the day.         Food Trucks!Come Take a Ne
 w Look at our Old Town!
GEO:35.476994;-76.811651
LOCATION:Historic Bath
SUMMARY:Patriots at Sea: An American Seaport Prepares for War
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/patriots-at-sea-an-american-
 seaport-prepares-for-war
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042642Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207083018532
DTSTART:20260725T140000Z
DTEND:20260725T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for sur
 vival\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fight
 s back in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the 
 world with unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with tr
 ippy toads\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover h
 ow these defenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage an
 d mimicry\, specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink
  bombs\, caboose cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, st
 and their ground or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live ani
 mal encounters\, larger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and 
 interactive programs.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of al
 l ages. Offered in English & Spanish.
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
