DESCRIPTION:In honor of World Ranger Day\, join a ranger at Boone Fork Park
 ing Area (milepost 299.9 on the Blue Ridge Parkway) for a short stroll alo
 ng the Tanawha Trail. Learn what rangers do on a day-to-day basis\, how we
  got our job\, and feel free to ask us questions! This short\, 1/4 mile ea
 sy hike ends at a beautiful bridge over the Boone Fork Creek. Feel free to
  continue your hike onto Grandfather Mountain State Park trails from here\
 , or turn around and walk back with the Ranger. \n\nPlease wear appropriat
 e hiking shoes and dress for the weather.\n\nThere are no bathrooms at Boo
 ne Fork Parking Area.
