X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042642Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52877655491505
DTSTART:20260803T140000Z
DTEND:20260803T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:Its that time of year again! Come celebrate the summer at Merch
 ants Millpond State Park with our 4th year of the Summer Junior Adventure 
 Series! In this series\, we have a different topic that we teach about eve
 ry Monday at 10 AM throughout the summer. \n\nThis week we'll talk about a
 nimals and their camouflage! We know that animals come in all different co
 lors\, but this often correlates with their environment. For most animals\
 , the best way to stay safe is to never be seen at all! Whether its hiding
  from predators or setting up an ambush\, camouflage plays an important ro
 le in the animal kingdom\, so come out to the Millpond and learn about som
 e of our creatures and their clever camouflage! \n\nThis program is for al
 l ages. We will begin promptly at 10 AM at the visitor center. Guests are 
 encouraged to dress for the weather as some of this program may be outside
 .
GEO:36.437278;-76.701271
LOCATION:Merchants Millpond State Park\, Visitor Center
SUMMARY:Ranger Alan's Clever Camouflage
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ranger-alans-clever-camoufla
 ge
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042642Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52903770452580
DTSTART:20260803T150000Z
DTEND:20260803T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Guided tours of Fort Macon are available daily at 11:00 a.m.\, 
 1:00 p.m.\, and 3:00 p.m. during the summer season from mid April to mid O
 ct.\n\nOn Cannon days there will only be one Fort Tour scheduled at 12:00 
 noon. \n\nTours last about 45 minutes.\n\nMeet at the fort entrance. Pets 
 are not allowed inside the fort.\n\n \n\nPhoto by C. Peek: The fort at For
 t Macon State Park
