X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042642Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52504709720826
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DESCRIPTION:Pretend you’ve been recruited as a member of the Culper Spy R
 ing\, and you need to know how to decipher a message written in invisible 
 ink. Supplies include a paint brush\, water\, drying cloth\, vitriol (dilu
 ted sulfuric acid)\, Thomas Jefferson cipher and “furnace box.” Read t
 he clues to find the coin with a hidden message\, reveal the message using
  the brush and vitriol\, then use the cipher to decode the message.\n\nCon
 tact: Nancy Locquet Absillis\, nancy.locquet@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SUMMARY: Spy Training 101: Decode a Secret Message
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/spy-training-101-decode-a-se
 cret-message
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042642Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52702202790114
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DESCRIPTION:May 2–August 9\, 2026\n\nEast Building\, Level B\, Meymandi E
 xhibition Gallery\n\nKnowing the West embraces and reexamines perceptions 
 of the American West to create more inclusive and complex dialogues. The e
 xhibition reflects the diverse perspectives that have contributed to art a
 nd life in the region. Presenting Native American works together with art 
 by non-Native makers\, it reveals how the stories we tell and the visual l
 anguage we employ influence understanding of our nation’s history and cu
 ltures.
GEO:35.807856;-78.703922
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art
SUMMARY:Knowing the West
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/knowing-the-west
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042642Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52949644644151
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DESCRIPTION:Save the Date!\n\nNC’s Route to Victory in the Revolution: Th
 e Race to the Dan\nAugust 7–8\, 2026\n\nJoin us for a two-day commemorat
 ion exploring North Carolina’s critical role in the Revolutionary War du
 ring the Winter Campaign of 1781. Through keynote presentations\, living h
 istory\, reenactments\, and historical interpretation\, this event will hi
 ghlight the events and people connected to “The Race to the Dan\,” a p
 ivotal campaign that helped lead to the British surrender at Yorktown late
 r that year.\n\nFriday\, August 7\, 2026\nBethania\, North Carolina\n\nThe
  opening day will feature a historical program and keynote address in the 
 historic Moravian community of Bethania\, followed by a reception at the C
 ornwallis House (c. 1770).\n\nFeatured Historians:\n• Dr. Wayne Lee\, UN
 C–Chapel Hill\, West Point Military Chair\n• Dr. Zachary Deibel\, Virg
 inia Military Institute\n\nSaturday\, August 8\, 2026\nShallow Ford State 
 Historic Site – Lewisville\, North Carolina\n\nThe second day will inclu
 de reenactments\, living history demonstrations\, a keynote address\, and 
 luncheon programming at the historic crossing site of Shallow Ford.\n\nFea
 tured Historian:\n• Dr. Troy Kickler\, NC Semiquincentennial Committee\n
 \nSponsored by the Bethania Historical Association\, The Conservation Fund
 \, Lewisville Historical Society\, and the NC Society of Cincinnati\, with
  assistance from the NC Historic Sites Division.\n\nMore details to come.
GEO:36.180889;-80.339793
LOCATION:Bethania Historical Association
SUMMARY:NC's Route to Victory in the Revolution: The Race to the Dan
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ncs-route-to-victory-in-the-
 revolution-the-race-to-the-dan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042642Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52745325337095
DTSTART:20260807T110000Z
DTEND:20260808T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunt at Elk Knob Sta
 te Park. Journey through northern hardwood forest\, follow winding mountai
 n trails\, and explore the unique ecosystems of this high-elevation park. 
 Keep your eyes open—what signs of wildlife or weather-shaped landscapes 
 will you uncover? Look for unique rocks that make Elk Knob a very special 
 clue in North Carolina’s geologic history. Start at the Visitor Center a
 nd scan the QR code in your Actionbound app. Flyers with the QR code will 
 be placed in the Park Office and on all park map kiosks. \n\nThe adventure
 s are available on the Actionbound app – a free download to your cellpho
 ne through your phone’s app store. There’s no need to create a profile
  and no personal data is collected with Actionbound. You simply find new h
 unts by searching for the park name or scanning the associated QR code pos
 ted for your park’s adventure.\n\nThis program is made possible through 
 a partnership with the NC Science Trail (ncsciencetrail.org)! Visit their 
 website for more Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunts being held in oth
 er NC State Parks and for other programs being offered throughout the stat
 e. \n\nThis scavenger hunt is running now through August 31\, 2026.
GEO:36.333462;-81.696432
LOCATION:Elk Knob State Park
SUMMARY:Elk Knob State Park: Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunt
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/elk-knob-state-park-curious-
 minds-adventure-scavenger-hunt
