BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042642Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52543890011455
DTSTART:20260815T140000Z
DTEND:20260815T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:We're going back to our roots.\n\nThis season\, Hickory Ridge H
 istory Museum proudly reintroduces Living History Museum Days\, a return t
 o the immersive\, hands-on spirit that once defined us as Hickory Ridge Li
 ving History Museum and “village”. On select days this summer\, the ca
 bins will come alive with the sights\, sounds\, and smells of 18th-century
  life in the North Carolina mountains.\n\nFrom open-hearth cooking and bla
 cksmithing to weaving\, spinning\, woodworking\, and frontier chores\, gue
 sts will experience a day in the life of the early settlers who called thi
 s region home. Our interpreters and volunteers will demonstrate traditiona
 l skills throughout the village\, inviting you to explore\, ask questions\
 , and connect with the everyday stories of Appalachian history.\n\nWhether
  you’re a longtime visitor or discovering us for the first time\, Living
  History Museum Days are your chance to step deeper into the past and to b
 e part of its future.\n\nInterested in volunteering or learning an 18th-ce
 ntury skill? We’re always looking for new hands to help bring the holler
  to life. Reach out to learn more about becoming part of SAHA family!
GEO:36.208683;-81.669982
LOCATION:Hickory Ridge History Museum
SUMMARY:Living History Museum Days at Hickory Ridge History Museum in Boone
 \, NC
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/living-history-museum-days-a
 t-hickory-ridge-history-museum-in-boone-nc
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042642Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207083038006
DTSTART:20260815T140000Z
DTEND:20260815T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for sur
 vival\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fight
 s back in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the 
 world with unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with tr
 ippy toads\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover h
 ow these defenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage an
 d mimicry\, specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink
  bombs\, caboose cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, st
 and their ground or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live ani
 mal encounters\, larger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and 
 interactive programs.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of al
 l ages. Offered in English & Spanish.
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
