DESCRIPTION:Learn about one of the small arms (musket\, flintlock\, or rifl
 e) that a soldier stationed at Fort Macon would have carried and used.\n\n
 This will include a blank firing demonstration of the weapon.\nMeet in the
  fort parade ground.\n\nDemonstrations will be at 10:30 a.m. and 2:30 p.m.
  every Saturday and Sunday (except Cannon Days) of June\, July\, and Aug.\
 n\nPhoto by Jairus Hill : Living historian demonstrating a musket at Fort 
 Macon State Park.
GEO:34.696366;-76.684506
LOCATION:Fort Macon State Park\, Ft. Macon
SUMMARY:Small Arms Demonstration 10:30 a.m. & 2:30 p.m.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/small-arms-demonstration-103
 0-am-230-pm
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
