BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042643Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52923395613309
DTSTART:20260904T130000Z
DTEND:20260904T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:We are proud to be a Blue Star Museum [again] in 2026! Active m
 ilitary personnel and up to five family members can visit the CSS Neuse Mu
 seum for free from May 16 (Armed Forces Day) through September 7 (Labor Da
 y). We appreciate your service and can’t wait for you to visit! \n\nBlue
  Star Museums is a partnership between the National Endowment for the Arts
  and Blue Star Families\, in collaboration with the Department of War and 
 museums across America\, offering free admission to the nation’s active-
 duty military personnel and their families\, including National Guard and 
 Reserve. \n\nHere is a link to other museums in North Carolina that partic
 ipate in the Blue Star Museums program: https://www.arts.gov/blue-star-mus
 eums-map?state=NC#bsm-map \;\n\nIf you have any questions\, please call 25
 2-526-9600\, ext. 221.
GEO:35.260403;-77.581573
LOCATION:CSS Neuse Civil War Museum
SUMMARY:Blue Star Museum Summer Program 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/blue-star-museum-summer-prog
 ram
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Special Site Programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042643Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52903770527365
DTSTART:20260904T150000Z
DTEND:20260904T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Guided tours of Fort Macon are available daily at 11:00 a.m.\, 
 1:00 p.m.\, and 3:00 p.m. during the summer season from mid April to mid O
 ct.\n\nOn Cannon days there will only be one Fort Tour scheduled at 12:00 
 noon. \n\nTours last about 45 minutes.\n\nMeet at the fort entrance. Pets 
 are not allowed inside the fort.\n\n \n\nPhoto by C. Peek: The fort at For
 t Macon State Park
GEO:34.696366;-76.684506
LOCATION:Fort Macon State Park\, Ft. Macon
SUMMARY:Fort Macon Daily Tours - 11 am\, 1 pm\, & 3 pm
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/fort-macon-daily-tours-11-am
 -1-pm-3-pm
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Guided Tours
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042643Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52912435038676
DTSTART:20260904T223000Z
DTEND:20260905T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join a ranger for an evening/night hike along the 3.5 mile Elli
 ott Couse Nature Trail.  Along with getting some unique views of the sunse
 t\, we will also be talking about\, and looking out for\, some of the diff
 erent creatures active at night that call Ft. Macon home.   Meet at the Ba
 thhouse and please park in the first (West) parking area as there will be 
 an astronomy event happening in the other parking lot when we return.
GEO:34.696366;-76.684506
LOCATION:Fort Macon State Park\, Beach Access / Bathhouse Parking Area (Pic
 nic Park Dr.)
SUMMARY:Night Hike
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/night-hike-930
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Outdoor Recreation (kayak\, paddle\, hikes)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042643Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52912376944518
DTSTART:20260905T010000Z
DTEND:20260905T023000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us and the Crystal Coast Stargazers at the beach access / 
 bathhouse parking area to view space through a telescope and learn more ab
 out our universe.\n\nThis event is dependent on clear weather and may be c
 anceled due to rain or heavy cloud cover. If you have a telescope\, feel f
 ree to bring it. Pets are not permitted at this program. \n\nIf you are no
 t setting up equipment for observations we ask that you park in the west p
 arking lot as you first enter\, then walk across to the east lot for the p
 rogram.  This helps reduce the amount of bright lights in the observation 
 area from headlights. \n\n \n\nPhoto by P. Terry: Star trails over a canno
 n at Fort Macon State Park
GEO:34.696366;-76.684506
LOCATION:Fort Macon State Park\, Beach Access / Bathhouse Parking Area (Pic
 nic Park Dr.)
SUMMARY:Astronomy
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/astronomy-3145
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Nature & Wildlife Programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042643Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52504709755671
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260905
DESCRIPTION:Pretend you’ve been recruited as a member of the Culper Spy R
 ing\, and you need to know how to decipher a message written in invisible 
 ink. Supplies include a paint brush\, water\, drying cloth\, vitriol (dilu
 ted sulfuric acid)\, Thomas Jefferson cipher and “furnace box.” Read t
 he clues to find the coin with a hidden message\, reveal the message using
  the brush and vitriol\, then use the cipher to decode the message.\n\nCon
 tact: Nancy Locquet Absillis\, nancy.locquet@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SUMMARY: Spy Training 101: Decode a Secret Message
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/spy-training-101-decode-a-se
 cret-message
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042643Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52399563439720
DTSTART:20260905T123000Z
DTEND:20260905T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Village of Pinehurst will be displaying two of the NC Depar
 tment of Natural & Cultural Resources exhibits throughout 2026.\n\n"Forgin
 g a Nation" will be on display at the Cannon Park Community Center\, 210 R
 attlesnake Trail\, Pinehurst\, NC 28374.\n\n"People of Colonial North Caro
 lina" will be on display at Assembly Hall\, 395 Magnolia Rd.\, Pinehurst\,
  NC 28374.\n\nThe Given Memorial Library & Tufts Archives (150 Cherokee Ro
 ad\, Pinehurst\, NC 28374) will also have smaller versions of the exhibits
  on display throughout the year and will rotate between the different exhi
 bit subjects periodically.
GEO:35.203585;-79.459138
LOCATION:Village of Pinehurst
SUMMARY:Village of Pinehurst NCDNCR America 250 Exhibits
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/village-of-pinehurst-ncdncr-
 america-250-exhibits
