DTSTART:20261114T150000Z
DTEND:20261114T173000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Indigenous Workshop - America 250 NC\,  introduces beginner
 s to the key steps and records that can unlock the  history of Black India
 ns. Whether you’ve never started your search or you’ve hit a roadblock
 \, you’ll learn how to make progress with confidence.\n\nIn this Native 
 American History Month presentation\, you’ll learn how to:\n\nBegin your
  family history journey using records that are free and easy to access onl
 ine.Find ancestors’ Tribal Rolls and Native American Records — and und
 erstand what those records reveal.Use clues from 1870 and beyond to trace 
 family lines further back in time.Overcome challenges created by the Trail
 s of Tears\, Slavery\,  and Segregation-era record keeping.You’ll see ho
 w ordinary documents — from Rolls and Census lists to Freedmen’s Burea
 u papers —   can tell extraordinary family stories.\n\nDeLoatch shares p
 ractical examples from his own research\, showing how he traced his ancest
 ry from Africa back 400 years to relatives enslaved in America.   Sponsore
 d by the AFRO-AMERICAN HISTORICAL & GENEALOGICAL SOCIETY\, INC (AAHGS\, In
 c.)\, North Carolina/Piedmont-Triad Chapter
GEO:36.075685;-79.787776
LOCATION:Greensboro History Museum\, Auditorium
SUMMARY:BLACK INDIANS: "Native American Family Research"
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/black-indians-native-america
 n-family-research
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042643Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52543890013505
DTSTART:20261114T150000Z
DTEND:20261114T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:We're going back to our roots.\n\nThis season\, Hickory Ridge H
 istory Museum proudly reintroduces Living History Museum Days\, a return t
 o the immersive\, hands-on spirit that once defined us as Hickory Ridge Li
 ving History Museum and “village”. On select days this summer\, the ca
 bins will come alive with the sights\, sounds\, and smells of 18th-century
  life in the North Carolina mountains.\n\nFrom open-hearth cooking and bla
 cksmithing to weaving\, spinning\, woodworking\, and frontier chores\, gue
 sts will experience a day in the life of the early settlers who called thi
 s region home. Our interpreters and volunteers will demonstrate traditiona
 l skills throughout the village\, inviting you to explore\, ask questions\
 , and connect with the everyday stories of Appalachian history.\n\nWhether
  you’re a longtime visitor or discovering us for the first time\, Living
  History Museum Days are your chance to step deeper into the past and to b
 e part of its future.\n\nInterested in volunteering or learning an 18th-ce
 ntury skill? We’re always looking for new hands to help bring the holler
  to life. Reach out to learn more about becoming part of SAHA family!
GEO:36.208683;-81.669982
LOCATION:Hickory Ridge History Museum
SUMMARY:Living History Museum Days at Hickory Ridge History Museum in Boone
 \, NC
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/living-history-museum-days-a
 t-hickory-ridge-history-museum-in-boone-nc
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042643Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51225005650217
DTSTART:20261114T160000Z
DTEND:20261114T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Hidden Battleship is for the explorer at heart! Join us for an 
 afternoon on a unique\, behind-the-scenes tour of unrestored areas on the 
 Battleship. Organized into small groups\, the participants are led to area
 s in the bow\, third deck\, and below\, and the superstructure\, including
  all the way to the very top! This program requires climbing ladders\, cro
 ssing high hatches\, and going through tight/confined spaces. The tour is 
 limited to ages 16 and older.\n\n2026 Dates\n\n► January 24\n► Februar
 y 28\n► March 28\n► April 18\n► November 14\n\n11 am – 5 pm\; $75 
 (plus tax) per participant. This program always sells out\, so get your Hi
 dden Battleship ticket now! This program is for ages 16 and older.
GEO:34.236158;-77.953643
LOCATION: Battleship North Carolina
SUMMARY:Hidden Battleship Tour
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/hidden-battleship-tour
END:VEVENT
