DTEND:20261216T203000Z
DESCRIPTION:Become more Bear Wise and learn all about black bears physical 
 features\, behavioral patterns\, and how they change with age. We will als
 o learn about prevention methods for both backcountry and rural settings\,
  alongside what to do if you encounter a bear in either setting. The Black
  Bear program will be held at The Seven Devils Community Center as part of
  their Ranger Workshop Series.
GEO:36.1557;-81.799301
LOCATION:Seven Devils Community Center
SUMMARY:Ranger Workshop - Black Bears
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ranger-workshop-black-bears
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Nature & Wildlife Programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260522T042644Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52808360219931
DTSTART:20261216T230000Z
DTEND:20261217T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for the June meeting of the America 250 NC Virtu
 al Book Club! We will be discussing Daughters of Green Mountain Gap by Ter
 i M. Brown on December 16 at 6p.\n\nThis historical fiction novel\, based 
 in North Carolina\, tells a story of generations of a women in one local f
 amily. As natural learning vs university education clash in the two older 
 women\, what is the third to think? Who will she follow? Is either path co
 rrect? \n\nPlease read the book prior to the discussion. We recommend borr
 owing from your local library. \n\nFree and open to the public. No members
 hip required. Come to whichever book talks spark your interest. \n\nMeetin
 g Link\n\nMore Information\n\nSign up for an Email Reminder
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Virtual Book Club: Daughters of Green Mountain Gap by Teri M. Brown
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/copy-of-virtual-book-club-Da
 ughters-of-Green-Mountain
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Panels & Book Discussions
END:VEVENT
